        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The runway is shrinking, and the Toronto Blue Jays just ran it out of gas. <strong>A 12-4 demolition by the upstart White Sox on Friday</strong> has snapped any post-break hope, leaving the club at 45-52 and 11½ games back in the AL East. Manager John Schneider pleaded for momentum after the All-Star break, but the offense is still stuck in 26th place for runs per game, and the starting rotation holds a league-low 18 wins. Braden Montgomery drove in four for Chicago while Toronto's bats went silent again, extending a three-game losing streak that now leaves them with just 19.9% playoff odds. The clubhouse knows the truth: they're two and a half games from a wild-card spot but drowning under.500. <strong>Today's 3:07 PM ET rematch against the White Sox at Rogers Centre is the first real chance to stop the bleed before the July 24 trade deadline closes in.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 18, 2026"
      },
