      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Raptors",
        "body": "Summer League isn't about the final record, but it's about the spark that tells you what's coming. The Raptors closed their non-consolation run with a <strong>99-90 win over the Miami Heat</strong>, led by rookie Allen Graves, who poured in 23 points on 8-of-16 shooting, including 4-of-6 from three, while adding six rebounds, four assists, two blocks, a steal, and zero turnovers. Graves, the No. 19 pick from June's draft, finished Summer League with a 3-1 record but fell just five points short of the playoffs. At 46-36 and third in the Atlantic Division, the team's season is over, and now the focus shifts to how Graves evolves alongside Kyle Anderson, the lone free-agent acquisition groomed to mentor him. <strong>Graves saving his best for last signals a potential steal for the Raptors, and the real test begins in camp this August.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 18, 2026"
      },
